

### 🧠 **Module 1: Facial Recognition of Reference Photos**

| Task                       | Tool/Service                                                        | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Face detection & embedding | **Google Cloud Vision API** or **Google Vertex AI (Custom Vision)** | Cloud Vision can detect faces but does **not provide embeddings**. You'll need a **custom model hosted on Vertex AI** or an open-source model hosted on GCP (e.g., TensorFlow\.js model in Node.js or C#-wrapped model). |
| Processing uploads         | **Cloud Functions** or **App Engine**                               | Trigger processing on photo upload.                                                                                                                                                                                      |
| Upload handling            | **Cloud Storage**                                                   | Store reference photos here. Integrate it with Cloud Functions or your backend for further processing.                                                                                                                   |

**Preferred Strategy:**

* Use **Google Cloud Storage** to store reference photos.
* Write a **C# or Node.js backend** that:

  * Calls **Google Vision API** for face detection (to crop faces).
  * Generates embeddings using a **local model** (like `face-api.js` in Node or a .NET wrapper around ONNX/TF).
  * Stores embeddings in a vector DB (see Module 2).

